DA  - 2026/02/03/
AB  - We present a lexicon of 214 textual markers of frustration in learner turns of text-based tutoring dialogues, grouped into six categories. Markers were derived from 1,800 annotated dialogues and validated against in-session self-reports from 240 learners. A simple marker count correlated with self-reported frustration at r = 0.47, comparable to a fine-tuned classifier (r = 0.52) and far more interpretable. Repetition of a prior question with added negation was the single strongest marker.
