N1  - <div data-schema-version="9"><h1>ISE 6664 project - frustration in AI tutoring transcripts</h1><p><span class="citation" data-citation="%7B%22citationItems%22%3A%5B%7B%22uris%22%3A%5B%22http%3A%2F%2Fzotero.org%2Fusers%2Flocal%2FmyLibrary%2Fitems%2FM776BWFS%22%5D%7D%5D%7D">(<span class="citation-item">Albrecht and Nwosu, 2022</span>)</span> use their 6 categories as our first-pass codebook, adapted to code tutoring.</p><ul><li>repetition w negation strongest marker (OR 3.9). in our transcripts this looks like re-asking the assistant the same thing w &quot;no&quot; / &quot;still&quot;</li><li>terse replies ambiguous -&gt; baseline per learner (Jordan&#x27;s idea of z-scoring reply length per student)</li><li>r = 0.47 for marker counts, transformer 0.52. we don&#x27;t have self-reports so we validate against our own hand labels instead</li></ul><p>split: Maya takes lexicon adaptation, Jordan the per-student baselines, me the transcript sampling + coding tool</p></div>
