AB  - Detectors of negative affect in tutoring logs often merge confusion and frustration. We annotated 6,200 learner turns from a chat-based statistics tutor with separate labels and found that the two states have different textual signatures and different consequences: confusion followed by a resolving explanation predicted higher post-test scores, while frustration did not. A detector that separates the two improves the usefulness of affect-triggered interventions.
