N1  - <div data-schema-version="9"><p><span class="citation" data-citation="%7B%22citationItems%22%3A%5B%7B%22uris%22%3A%5B%22http%3A%2F%2Fzotero.org%2Fusers%2Flocal%2FmyLibrary%2Fitems%2FEQRTZG28%22%5D%7D%5D%7D">(<span class="citation-item">Gallo and Stein, 2023</span>)</span> key distinction for our codebook: confusion != frustration. resolved confusion is GOOD (6 pt post-test gain), frustration is not.</p><ul><li>confused cues: &quot;but&quot;, hedges, restating. frustrated: repetition, giving up, complaining about the tutor</li><li>they label &quot;both&quot; (230 turns). we should allow both too</li><li>Dr. Brooks will like this for the theory section (link to appraisal stuff from lecture 5)</li></ul></div>
