AB  - Learning software is full of failure: wrong answers, failed tests, broken builds. We reviewed 41 learning applications and interviewed 12 designers to collect patterns for the moment after a learner fails. We describe nine patterns, from "name the next smallest step" to "make the failure cheap to retry", and discuss their affective rationale with reference to broaden-and-build theory and emotional design.
